2.2.0
DIRECT-MONKEYPATCH
- Rebuild the MUSIC tab as a lean, station-based persistent player modeled on
  the device's proven custom RADIO ("mojave") tab. Pick a station folder from
  MUSIC/ and it keeps playing across the whole Pip-Boy OS (STATS / INV / DATA /
  MAP / RADIO) and the terminal's own screens - like the built-in radio.
- Persistence engine is installed as closure-free new Function() wrappers on
  Pip / Pip.radio, so it survives the scene being torn down. While playing,
  Pip.audioStart / Pip.audioStop ignore foreign (OS) calls so the per-screen
  CRT static can't cut the music; an audioStopped handler + a watchdog advance
  tracks. State is RAM-only, so a reboot / power-off stops it like any app.
- Wrap Pip.goToSleep so audio stops cleanly before the device sleeps.
- Stop playback by pressing the playing station again, via STOP RADIO on the
  media menu, or it stops on sleep / power-off.
- Relaunching the terminal while music is playing skips the intro and returns to
  the media selection menu with the music still going.
- Add SETTINGS to the first-page media menu.
- Kept the MUSIC scene small (~9 KB vs ~19 KB) so the resident + peak RAM stays
  close to the mojave tab, which the device runs without LOW_MEMORY. Video and
  image viewers stay as their own separate scenes.

